## Core Services

### 1. Cognitive Behavioral Therapy for Insomnia (CBT-I)
- **What it is**: The gold-standard, non-pharmacological first-line treatment for chronic insomnia, endorsed by the American Academy of Sleep Medicine (AASM) and the American College of Physicians (ACP).
- **Structure**: 6–8 structured, time-limited weekly sessions.
- **Key Components**:
  - Sleep restriction & stimulus control therapy (retraining the brain's association between bed and sleep).
  - Cognitive restructuring (replacing racing catastrophic thoughts and sleep anxiety).
  - Relaxation training and nervous system arousal reduction.
  - Sleep medication tapering support (coordinating with client prescribers).
  - Relapse prevention planning.
- **Efficacy**: ~80% of individuals with chronic insomnia experience significant, lasting improvements.
- **URL (EN)**: https://greywellness.com/en/pages/sleep/
- **URL (ES)**: https://greywellness.com/es/pages/sleep/

### 2. Anxiety Therapy
- **Modality**: Cognitive Behavioral Therapy (CBT) and Mindfulness-Based Stress Reduction (MBSR).
- **Target Population**: Adults struggling with racing thoughts, somatic anxiety, nighttime panic, and chronic stress.
- **URL (EN)**: https://greywellness.com/en/pages/anxiety/
- **URL (ES)**: https://greywellness.com/es/pages/anxiety/

### 3. Trauma Therapy & Cognitive Processing Therapy (CPT)
- **Modality**: Cognitive Processing Therapy (CPT) and trauma-informed counseling.
- **Structure**: Typically 7–13 structured sessions.
- **URL (EN)**: https://greywellness.com/en/pages/trauma/
- **URL (ES)**: https://greywellness.com/es/pages/trauma/

